Dear Robert,

I have completed a review of the latest thickness data for ATU-100 following the Larkhall NDE Services Inc. survey, LNDE-RPT-20160118-004-R0. Short-term corrosion rates on the rich amine circuits have increased since 2011, which aligns with the higher acid-gas loading predictions documented in QSCP-DMR-2014-002. Specifically, lines 4-RA-101, 4-RA-102, and the 6-RA-103 header show accelerated thinning, though all readings currently remain above the 3.81 mm and 4.57 mm t-min thresholds.

The increased rates on the rich side of the L/R exchanger, 4-RA-104, confirm the necessity of the 3-year inspection interval established during the MOC. Please ensure the Unit Engineer, Robert Hendricks, is aware that these short-term rates will now dictate the remaining life calculations and subsequent inspection scheduling for these assets.

Regards, Jennifer Walsh

Jennifer Walsh, Inspection Coordinator, API 570 inspector, QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department